#N five-margolus-media.rle
#O Connor Steppie, 10 January 2018
#C period-4094 block automaton XOR oscillators
#C Source:
#C   https://conwaylife.com/forums/viewtopic.php?p=54909#p54909
#C
#C This pattern shows a simulation of high-period XOR oscillators in the
#C "MarBlocks" family, using 2×2 regions in an isotropic non-totalistic
#C (INT) rule. Refer to comparison.rle for an explanation of the
#C MarBlocks family of oscillators.
#C
#C In this case, all five possible "MarBlocks media" actually coexist
#C in a single rule: blocks can be filled, 3/4 filled, 1/2 filled
#C (in two different ways), or 1/4 filled.  Many INT rules can emulate
#C Margolus rules with one or the other of these methods, but rules
#C that allow all of the methods simultaneously are much rarer.
#C
#C The related rule B2c3iny4aikt5iny6c/S2c3iny4aikt5iny6c effectively
#C emulates four non-interacting universes of the 1/4-filled variant,
#C making the coexistence of these five media trivial.
#C
#C For various MarBlocks media, see
#C  https://conwaylife.com/forums/viewtopic.php?f=11&t=5204
x = 94, y = 54, rule = B2c3i4i5i/S2c3i4i5iHistory
44A6.44A$44A6.A.A.A.A.A.A.A.A.A.A.A.A.A.A.A.A.A.A.A.A.A.A26$25.44A25$
